cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use seleCte in your research, please cite the FDG 2025 paper below
  rather than the software itself.
title: seleCte
abstract: >-
  Procedural generation of playable Celeste levels. A multi-dimensional Markov
  chain trained on the tile patterns of the game's own rooms fills the rooms of a
  procedurally drawn level skeleton, which is then encoded back into a binary map
  the game can load.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Louis
    family-names: Robinet
repository-code: "https://github.com/robilouis/seleCte"
license: MIT
version: 0.10.0
keywords:
  - procedural content generation
  - level generation
  - platformer
  - markov chain
  - game ai
  - celeste
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
